cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CoronaryCCO.jl: a vendor-neutral, GPU-accelerated Julia port of HCT-CCO
  for subject-specific coronary arterial tree generation
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the HCT-CCO article and the OpenCCO
  article listed under references, as well as this software. CoronaryCCO.jl
  is a port; the method belongs to the upstream authors.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
authors:
  - given-names: Dale
    family-names: Black
    affiliation: University of California, Irvine — Molloi Lab
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9150-9827
repository-code: https://github.com/MolloiLab/CoronaryCCO.jl
url: https://github.com/MolloiLab/CoronaryCCO.jl
abstract: >-
  Pure-Julia port of HCT-CCO (Hierarchy CT-Driven Constrained Constructive
  Optimization), which grows subject-specific coronary arterial trees from a
  segmented epicardial base tree inside a CT-derived myocardial domain. Kernels
  are written with AcceleratedKernels.jl and KernelAbstractions.jl so the same
  code runs on multithreaded CPUs and on CUDA, ROCm, oneAPI and Metal GPUs. The
  port targets bit-identical trees relative to the upstream C++ implementation
  given the same candidate-point stream.
keywords:
  - constrained constructive optimization
  - coronary arteries
  - vascular tree generation
  - Julia
  - GPU
